activation	Interpolate variables and render templates	2026-10-27T11:20:50.4558173Z   GH_AW_STEPS_PREPARE_OUTPUTS_ISSUE: {"title": "duckdb 1.4.4 (node-duckdb): complete WAL fails to replay with \"Conflict on tuple deletion\" on reopen", "body": "## Environment\n\n- duckdb 1.4.4 via node-duckdb (node-v20.20.2, Linux WSL2)\n- single-process embedded use\n- `.duckdb` file (536,576 B) + `.duckdb.wal` file (12,873 B)\n\n## Symptoms\n\nA specific `.duckdb` + `.wal` pair fails **deterministically** (3/3 reproducible in a fresh process) with:\n```\nTransactionContext Error: Failure while replaying WAL file \"\u2026/org_<id>.duckdb.wal\": Conflict on tuple deletion!\n```\n\nThe `.duckdb` file opens cleanly when the `.wal` is absent.\n\n## Details\n\nThe pair was captured from a live workload after a `Database` instance closed and immediately reopened (gap ~100 ms). At the time of close, no transactions were in flight (`liveConns=0`, no pending write tasks). The WAL is complete \u2014 byte-identical from close to reopen, 12,873 B of payload with no zero-filled tail.\n\n**WAL contents** (SQL-level operations):\n- 14\u00d7 `ALTER TABLE \u2026 ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` \u2014 schema evolution, idempotent operations\n- 5\u00d7 `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS` \u2014 index creation, idempotent operations\n- Multiple DELETE and INSERT statements on the same table \u2014 row-level mutations\n\n**Minimal-repro attempt:**\nA synthetic stress script exercising DDL + DELETE cycling, run through 6 un-checkpointed close/reopen cycles with WALs up to 400 KB, replays fine in all variants. The unreplayable condition is more specific than the DDL+DELETE pattern alone.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. Is a complete WAL that replays into a \"Conflict on tuple deletion\" error expected to be recoverable?\n2. Is `CHECKPOINT` on close required for correctness in embedded use, or is this a defect in WAL recovery?\n3. Does WAL replay validate the main file's metadata before attempting to apply operations, and could a stale metadata mismatch cause this error?\n\n## Attachments\n\nThe `.duckdb` (536,576 B) + `.duckdb.wal` (12,873 B) pair and a Node reproduction script (`require(\"duckdb\")` only) are preserved and can be provided on request \u2014 the repository they live in is private. Comment here and I will attach them.\n\n---\n\n**Context:** We encounter this as part of a multi-tenant analytics system where Database instances are closed and reopened frequently per organization (fire-and-forget close pattern). A checkpoint before close avoids the issue entirely. The main file opens and queries cleanly without the WAL, so the inconsistency is between the WAL's entries and the main file's state at replay time.\n\n---\n\nFiled from the investigation of upstream reference treilly/autometrik number 1528 (fix merged as PR upstream reference  number 2304); happy to run any additional diagnostics against the pair.\n"}
